// forge_country -- ISO 3166-1 country reference data + validation for address forms, dropdowns, shipping/tax
// logic, and phone country codes. Maps between alpha-2 code ("US"), alpha-3 code ("USA"), English name
// ("United States"), and telephone calling code ("1"). Every lookup uppercases + trims its input first, so
// "us", " Us ", "US" all resolve. The four tables are built once inside private helpers as dicts keyed by the
// canonical alpha-2 (or alpha-3 for the reverse map). Covers ~50 of the most common countries -- enough to be
// genuinely useful for real address/shipping forms without pretending to be the full 249-entry register.
// LEAF -- imports NOTHING.

